 Any `HINDSIGHT_API_*` variable you export is forwarded to the daemon, so server-side settings need
 no equivalent here.
 
+## Managed context (resident facade)
+
+Set `managedContext: true` when an external context authority owns injection,
+learning and source checks. The shared hook/runtime then performs no automatic
+recall, page roster/preamble, seed, survey, transcript write-back, package update or
+companion-skill synchronization. OpenCode 2 does not register the companion skill.
+The installer also skips new skill copies; use a dedicated runner profile without
+previously installed Hindsight skills, since this setting does not delete old copies.
+
+The only tool in this mode is `memory_search({query})`. It calls the configured
+facade's `/v1/search` with a fixed `managedScopeId`, using the existing authenticated
+HTTP transport. It sends no bank or caller-supplied scope/tags, refuses redirects,
+and returns the facade's advisory source/provenance envelope without the native page
+guide. Failure returns an explicit unavailable result, with no engine fallback.
+`memory_reflect`, source retrieval and learning writes are not exposed in this version.
+
+```json
+{
+  "managedContext": true,
+  "serverMode": "self-hosted",
+  "apiUrl": "http://127.0.0.1:8787",
+  "apiToken": "REPLACE_WITH_FACADE_READER_TOKEN",
+  "managedScopeId": "resident-world-main",
+  "optInOnly": true,
+  "optInPaths": ["/workspace/resident-world"]
+}
+```
+
+`apiUrl` must be an explicit HTTPS origin, or HTTP on `127.0.0.1`, `localhost` or
+`[::1]`, with no path, query, credentials or fragment. Queries are limited to 4096
+UTF-8 bytes; responses to 64 KiB, 256 entries and 64 source references per entry.
+Missing facade origin, scope, reader token or self-hosted mode exposes no
+tools. A managed configuration has no cloud URL default. Set `managedContext` and
+`managedScopeId` at the top level or in `harnesses.<name>`; bank/path overrides cannot
+change them. Existing project opt-in and native session ownership guards still apply.
+Keep this config outside the agent-writable workspace and restart persistent hosts
+after changes; the facade must enforce the token's scope independently.
+The reused HTTP transport retains the host's global dispatcher, including an
+installed proxy. Fixed origins and refused redirects do not bypass or qualify that
+dispatcher. Commission the runner's dispatcher, environment and OS egress policy
+before giving it even a reader token; this adapter does not establish host isolation.
+
 ## Configuration
 
 Configuration is **one JSON file**: `~/.hindsight/coding-agent.json`. Layering, later wins per field:
